# Keeps the build context (and therefore the image) free of anything that
# shouldn't ship in a layer. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` — without this,
# a real backend/.env sitting next to it at build time would get baked
# straight into the image. Real config always arrives at runtime via the
# environment, never from a file copied into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
